Ok, new versions.

1) Kusanagi, chaotic short sword (wakizashi)

     This blade was found by Susanowo when he slew Orochi, the 8-headed
dragon. He then gifted it to Amaterasu to redress an earlier wrong,
after which it found its way back to earth.

    Effects when wielded: grants poison resistance and 75% sickness
resistance, but DOES NOT cure existing sickness.
    On hit: +d5 to hit, double damage versus dragons, snakes, lizards
and other reptilians, 25% chance to scare air elementals and vortices
on successful
hit. (One of Kusanagi's powers is the ability to control wind and air).

I wasn't completely sure what kind of base weapon to make this - the
proper Japanese name for it includes the word 'Tsurugi', but I've never
seen it represented as one. It's often drawn as a katana, but most
scholars think it's more of a short, straight or slightly curved blade,
the katana being a rather newer design. Short sword, thus, makes the
most sense to me, but a case could be made for katana or scimitar, too.

2) Kanajana, neutral long sword

    (From Moorcock's Eternal Champion series, as the weapon of Erekose)
    When wielded: sheds light (like Sunsword).
     On hit: +d5 to hit, deals 1d6 extra damage to all enemies. Double
damage versus humanoids (all @, h, G plus nurses and lycanthropes. Also
versus Doppelgangers, Drow etc in [S]). 5% chance of an instakill
versus @s. (the radiation that Kanajana emits, per the
book, can be deadly to humans)
(extra damage applied /after/ doubling, like Grayswandir/Werebane's
silver damage)

3) Twinkle, unaligned scimitar (changed from chaotic. Drizzt is CG, but
the weapons he wields seem unaligned)

     (One of the weapons of Drizzt Do'Urden from R.A. Salvatore's
Forgotten Realms books. Possibly a copyright problem, alas, but if it's
not...)
    When wielded: Warning versus lawful foes, protection equal to
enchantment.
    On hit: +d5 to hit, +1d4 damage all the time, extra 1d6 damage if
two-weaponed in primary hand, double damage to (master) mind
flayers. (extra damage applied /after/ doubling, like
Grayswandir/Werebane's silver damage)

4) Katana of Masamune, lawful katana

     (From Japanese myth)
    When wielded: bisection/decapitation/artifact-instakill resistance
(from Tsurugi, Vorpal Blade, Kanajana, etc) (the Katana of Masamune
parries the fatal slash!)
    On hit: +d5 to hit against all foes, may (50% chance) destroy
enemy's (non-artifact) weapon, +1d6 versus living monsters.

5) Icingdeath, unaligned scimitar

    (Drizzt's other scimitar, powers based on the observed ones from
the novels)
    Wielded: Fire resistance, cold resistance.
    On hit: +d5 to hit, +1d6 versus non-cold-resistant foes, double
damage versus demons (cold damage applied after doubling), 20% chance
to slow lawful demons or stun chaotic demons.


Ok, hopefully this has fixed up any gimpy points without making things
